// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\drosemann\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":7,"newStart":8,"newLines":7,"lines":[" I have a lot of experience with the Pterodactyl and Coolify panels, but for my own services I now prefer pure Docker because it means less overhead and more control."," I have a lot of productive experience with MariaDB and I've tested Supabase extensively, both in the cloud and self hosted."," I use Cloudflare for DNS, HetrixTools for monitoring, Trello and Notion for project management for ShadowUnity, and Vercel for automatic deployments.","-My browser survival game stranded-horizons is the one project still on Vercel auto-deploys: https://github.com/drosemann/stranded-horizons","+My browser survival game stranded-horizons is the one project still on Vercel auto-deploys, a lightweight vanilla HTML, CSS and JavaScript wave survival game on HTML5 Canvas with WASD and mouse aim, coin-funded speed and damage upgrades and a localStorage highscore, with no backend and no build step: https://github.com/drosemann/stranded-horizons"," On the client side I use Windows, with a nod to the games industry, and I plan to switch to Linux as soon as anticheat support gets better."," My focus is on cybersecurity, AI, cloud and virtualization, and automation with Python."," For that Python side I built aktienwerk, which turns SEC filings and stock prices for 100 US companies into plain explanations with only the standard library and SQLite: https://github.com/drosemann/aktienwerk"]}]}]}
